  "summary": "Metal Slug 2 is SNK's run-and-gun sequel, first released for Neo Geo MVS in Japan on 23 February 1998.",
  "body": [
    "Metal Slug 2 is SNK's run-and-gun sequel, first released for Neo Geo MVS in Japan on 23 February 1998. Marco and Tarma return alongside Eri and Fio as General Morden's forces begin another campaign. One or two players move through densely animated stages, shooting enemies, collecting weapons and taking control of vehicles before confronting a large boss. The expanded squad accompanies a wider range of settings and transformations, carrying the original's comic military action towards a stranger conflict involving creatures and machines from beyond its familiar army.",
    "Prisoners rescued along the route provide weapons or other useful items. Reaching the end of a mission preserves them for a score bonus, while losing a life clears the current rescue tally. A successful run therefore means protecting progress as well as collecting it. Destructible scenery can conceal further supplies, encouraging shots beyond the obvious enemy targets. Tanks add weapons and protection, while close-range knife attacks handle opponents within reach. The player repeatedly moves between vulnerable infantry fighting and brief opportunities to command something much more powerful.",
    "Transformations alter the soldier's abilities during certain sections, making an unexpected condition part of handling the next obstacle. Helpers also appear: the rescued Hyakutaro can fight alongside the squad, while Rumi supplies additional items. These small encounters reinforce the animation's humour while providing practical assistance. Takushi Hiyamuta composed the music, continuing the series' energetic accompaniment. The original release also suffered substantial slowdown in busy scenes, leading to the later reworking Metal Slug X. The sequel established the larger cast and increasingly fantastical action that subsequent games would continue to expand."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "The squad grows",
    "A rescue worth protecting",
    "The battlefield becomes stranger"
  ],
